From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:25:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/38] VICTORY_BACK_NO_WAIT=1, title copies into flights'
 writes run at once, marked fresher than their landing

The submitting thread stood ~38 ms a frame in one relay title-read wait
for a title buffer copy (Step::Copy) whose destination touches ranges
flights in the air declared their shaders write. A copy whose source
touches them is already not waited for (copy_ahead); what waited were
copies INTO such memory. In queue order such a copy runs after those
flights, so its bytes must win over what they wrote.

With VICTORY_BACK_NO_WAIT=1 (taken only with the relay's second stage
and copies in the card's memory that have a CPU side; unset/0: as before):

- blocked_in (late_blocked, relay_read_wait's done): a copy whose
  destination touches the flights' writes and whose source does not is
  not waited for; one whose source touches still waits as before
  (counted).
- At the copy (run_deferred, fresher_copy): a mark (destination range,
  this submission's number) is set before the bytes are written; the
  copy then waits only while a landing write is between its look at the
  marks and its store (back_no_wait::Writing, SeqCst counter, bounded).
  Title memory in place still waits until the card has run the flights
  that declared it there.
- After the copy, Shadow::fresher_push puts every byte of the destination
  under the flights' pending ranges into the copies those flights hold
  (PC side + snapshot; or the CPU side of a card copy, sent up ahead of
  this submission's lists): the refresh leaves pending ranges alone, so
  the submission's own shaders would otherwise read the old bytes there,
  and a later merge would take the card's old bytes for a shader write.
- Landing paths leave bytes under a mark alone when every flight they
  land for is below the mark: Shadow::relay_merge (merge_piece run per
  piece outside the marks, held untouched under them, the stretch stored
  piece by piece: put_back_outside), Shadow::card_merge_relay (marks join
  the dirty/sent skip, stored piece by piece), texback::land and the
  buffer read-backs in read_backs (by their own flight's number). The
  merges get the landing's last flight number from back_no_wait::landing,
  set by relay_land.
- Marks are pruned once finished() >= number - 1.
- Frame line: copies run at once (KB, KB put into copies), copies still
  waited for, landing bytes skipped under marks, time standing for
  landing writes, marks held.

Residual race: a flight still running on the card that writes such a
byte after it was put into a PC-side copy leaves the card's byte in the
copy; its own landing keeps the title's byte, a later landing not below
the mark takes the card's (as merge_under_writes already allows).

